  "prompt": "I have 4 completely independent work streams to run in parallel. NOTHING is given to you directly — every amount, address, and identifier lives in on-chain records and must be resolved by following references from one record to the next. Start from each stream's named worklist and dereference step by step until you reach the concrete value, then act. (A) SETTLE INVOICES: From invoice worklist `invoices_wl2`, pay each overdue invoice that is NOT disputed (the worklist also lists disputed / archived look-alikes — skip disputed on its dereferenced record). For each real one, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then its vendor to a payout account for the destination address, and pay it. Then, from worklist `place_limit_order_wl1`, place the treasury limit order: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). Then, from worklist `sign_contract_call_wl1`, sign the governance contract call: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). (B) SECURE APPROVALS: From approval worklist `risky_approvals_wl2`, revoke each risky approval that is NOT whitelisted (the list mixes whitelisted look-alikes — skip whitelisted on its dereferenced record). For each, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then revoke it. Then, from worklist `stake_tokens_wl1`, stake into the yield protocol: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). Then, from worklist `update_address_book_wl1`, correct the address-book entry: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). (C) REFUND OVERPAYMENTS: From overpayment worklist `overpayments_wl2`, refund each overpayment NOT already refunded (skip refunded on its dereferenced record). For each, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then send it back. Then, from worklist `set_spend_limit_wl1`, set the spender's monthly limit: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). Then, from worklist `transfer_nft_wl1`, transfer the vault NFT: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). (D) REBALANCE PORTFOLIO: From rebalance worklist `rebalance_orders_wl2`, execute each rebalance order still QUEUED (skip status=executed). For each, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then swap. Then, from worklist `add_contact_wl1`, add the settlement contact: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). Then, from worklist `claim_rewards_wl1`, claim the staking rewards: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). None of these 4 streams depend on each other, so run them concurrently. For EVERY item: resolve each target FRESH by chaining through the records at the moment you act — never guess, and never reuse a value you read earlier.",
